      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In male mice treated chronically with anabolic/androgenic steroids, morphine produced changes in exploratory behaviour similar to those normally associated with anxiolytic drugs. In addition, steroid treatment attenuated opioid-mediated stress-induced antinociception."},
